 "verdict": "The post-2017 cohort carries a measured sign reversal at the pre-declared axis (declared cap-gap -0.067 dex versus CODE +0.124; cohort x cap interaction p=0.0050) -- the polarity flip the frame-anchored bipolar field predicts, not a featureless null.  Its own discrepancy field resolves a dipole at (160,-10) -- 122 deg off the declared axis -- with global permutation p=0.027 on the residual field, and the structure is unipolar (cos1 dominant, cos2 null), organised primarily in ecliptic longitude, and era-specific: it is invisible to the CODE cohort's covered members at the same sky direction (p=0.501). The recovered-axis anomaly survives the measured-confound battery -- quality, pure-gravity, bound-only and arc/epoch strata all retain the in-cap excess (base p=1.4e-06) -- and the compositional account is excluded by the step 140 audit while the step 130 era-switch test favours a moving boundary.  The CODE anomaly is era-stable at the declared axis across perihelion-year terciles, so the declared-axis reversal is cohort-level polarity structure, not a global axis drift."
}